{#
    One card, and the element draws all of it.

    **Every option is a property.** The directive says what the entry is — the
    title, where it goes, the kind, the date, the picture — and each of those
    lands on `sds-teaser` as an attribute. Nothing here says what a card looks
    like: not the frame, not the row above the title, not what a title is
    wrapped in. That is the whole point of there being a component. This
    template used to spell `.sds-teaser__body` and `.sds-teaser__title` because
    the element read its own parts back to find them, which made every internal
    name public API and left the element framing markup this file had already
    built — a card that could not be changed on one side without the other.

    What paid for that arrangement was the reader with no JavaScript, and it is
    not needed any more: `make guides` renders every element in the output ahead
    of the browser — `scripts/lib/prerender.ts` — so a property reaches a page
    that runs no script at all.

    The summary is the one thing still written between the tags, because it is
    the one thing an attribute cannot hold: out of a document a summary is
    paragraphs, and sometimes a list.

    The title is the link and the card is not. A card wrapped in one anchor
    announces its whole contents as that link's name, and takes selecting the
    text inside it away from the reader — so what is pressable is the line that
    says where pressing it goes, and the card follows on hover. Where there is
    nowhere to go, the element leaves the title a title.
#}
{#- The picture goes by the name every other directive that takes a file uses:
    what an option is called belongs to the language it is written in, and
    `.. figure::` and `.. image::` already gave the file that name.

    Resolved here and not in the element: what a path means is the renderer's
    business — which document it was written in, and whether it points out of
    the site — and the element is handed the URL that came of it. -#}
{%- set src = node.option('src') -%}
{%- set source = src ? (src is external_target ? src : asset(src)) : '' -%}
<sds-teaser
    heading="{{ node.option('title') }}"
    {%- if node.option('href') %} href="{{ renderLink(node.option('href')) }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('tag') %} tag="{{ node.option('tag') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('meta') %} meta="{{ node.option('meta') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if source %} src="{{ source }}" alt="{{ node.option('alt')|default('') }}"{% endif %}
>
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</sds-teaser>
